<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tsarevo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tsarevo is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, in Burgas Province near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strandzha">Strandzha</a> mountains. As Vasiliko it was a centre of the Strandzha Commune during the Preobrazhenie Uprising of 1903, and it passed to Bulgaria after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a>. It was renamed Tsarevo in 1934 and was called Michurin from 1950 to 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tsarevo.jpg" alt="Tsarevo" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SpaceControl · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tsarevo_-_panoramio_-_SpaceControl_(5).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
